ere cut back in size in Q3 2026.\n- **Spending response:** After the pulled offering, Pellham said it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and resize its Q1 2027 tender. That tender was about C$900M before the cut. Pellham had planned 2027 capital spending up 18%.\n- **Debt is also tighter:** Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. Debt is therefore a weaker fallback, not a cheap substitute for equity.\n- **Read-through:** The utilities cannot fund 2027 plans as filed through equity. Expect scaled-back, deferred or resized capex, mainly for transformers and substations. That is a negative for grid-equipment suppliers' 2027 orders.\n\n**Caveat:** I did not find Norvane's own equity plans or the full text of Pellham's market statement. This verdict rests mainly on Pellham, the largest buyer, and the Q3 offering tracker.\n\nSources: the Q3 2026 issuance tracker (`pellham-offering`), the 2027 tender calendar (`utility-tenders`) and the Q3 credit conditions note (`utility-credit`).","ttft_ms":2193,"type":"result","duration_ms":32870,"uuid":"e3ae55dd-aa9e-40cc-9d11-60c6828d7294","ttft_stream_ms":1694,"time_to_request_ms":58,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":5,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":8,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":58,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":205,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":132,"process_rss_mib_result":198,"process_anon_mib_result":116,"process_peak_rss_mib":223,"process_cpu_ms_turn":786,"process_wall_ms_turn":32870,"process_cpu_m